        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1002$",
          "worked": "The digit sums of $1001$ and $1002$ are $2$ and $3$, respectively. Thus $1001$ fails the test for $3$, and $1002$ is the first number greater than $1000$ that passes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1008$",
          "worked": "For $1001$ to $1007$, the last three digits represent $1$ to $7$, none divisible by $8$. The last three digits of $1008$ represent $8$, so $1008$ is the smallest required number.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1004$",
          "worked": "For $1001$, $1002$ and $1003$, the last two digits represent $1$, $2$ and $3$, which are not divisible by $4$. The last two digits of $1004$ represent $4$, so the answer is $1004$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1002$",
          "worked": "$1001$ is odd, so it is not divisible by $6$. The next number, $1002$, is even and has digit sum $3$. It is divisible by both $2$ and $3$, hence by $6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$3$ and $4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1008$",
          "worked": "The first numbers greater than $1000$ divisible by $4$ are $1004$ and $1008$. Their digit sums are $5$ and $9$, respectively. Only $1008$ is also divisible by $3$, so it is the smallest required number.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$3$, $4$ and $5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1020$",
          "worked": "Divisibility by $5$ requires a last digit of $0$ or $5$. Divisibility by $4$ also requires an even number, so the last digit must be $0$. The first candidates above $1000$ are $1010$ and $1020$. Their last two digits are $10$ and $20$; only $1020$ passes the test for $4$. Its digit sum is $3$, so it also passes the test for $3$. The answer is $1020$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
